### Assertion Support
<hr class="section-rule lvl-3">

Without real typing or great static-analysis, `make` benefits from a few ways to write defensive code.  The precondition checks all live under the **`assert.*`** namespace and share one contract: they **pass quietly** when the condition holds and **fail loudly** (nonzero exit + a red log line) when it doesn't, so they compose naturally as recipe guards or target prerequisites.

The twin demos below exercise the passing path of each kind, **environment**, **tool**, and **stream** assertions, as [twins]({{_}}/cmk/compiler) (a plain `Makefile` and its [cmk-lang]({{_}}/cmk/compiler) equivalent; toggle the tabs).  The comments cover the macro-vs-target forms and what each guards against.

{{site.embed_mirror('demos/assertions.mk', 'demos/cmk/assertions.cmk', github=github, default='left')}}

Environment assertions also underpin the [argument-parsing support](#bind-from-environment): a kwarg mentioned without a default is implicitly required.

